IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act -- piece cp4: THE PENSION INDEX SERIES (infrastructure).
--
-- No provision of this piece's range licenses these rules. The flat rate benefits of sections 56(2),
-- 58(1.1), 59(1) and 59.2 are each worked out year by year from "the Pension Index for the year ...
-- bears to the Pension Index for the year preceding", and the Pension Index is the value of section
-- 43 (piece cp3), so it is supplied. The series is a list of NUMBER, one value per year, in order of
-- year, with the first entry the index for 1986 (the first year any cp4 flat rate benefit names).
-- A year the series does not reach, or an index of zero as a denominator, is NOTHING: the text does
-- not decide it.

§ `The Pension Index series`

-- Not a provision: the Pension Index for a year, read out of a series that begins with 1986.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      series IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp4 the Pension Index for a year in a series beginning with 1986` year series MEANS
    IF (year LESS THAN 1986) OR ((year MINUS 1986) AT LEAST (count series))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (at series (year MINUS 1986))

-- Not a provision: "the ratio that the Pension Index for the year ... bears to the Pension Index for
-- the year preceding that year".
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      series IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp4 the ratio of the Pension Index for a year to the Pension Index for the year before` year series MEANS
    CONSIDER `cp4 the Pension Index for a year in a series beginning with 1986` year series
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST thisYear THEN
        CONSIDER `cp4 the Pension Index for a year in a series beginning with 1986` (year MINUS 1) series
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST lastYear THEN
            IF lastYear EQUALS 0
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST (thisYear DIVIDED BY lastYear)

-- Not a provision: an amount multiplied by a ratio, either of which may be missing.
GIVEN amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      ratio IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp4 an amount that may be missing times a ratio that may be missing` amount ratio MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER ratio
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (a TIMES r)


-- Not a provision: "the ratio that the Pension Index for one year bears to the Pension Index for another",
-- from the two index values. A zero denominator is NOTHING: the text does not decide it.
GIVEN numerator IS A NUMBER
      denominator IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp4 the ratio of one Pension Index value to another` numerator denominator MEANS
    IF denominator EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (numerator DIVIDED BY denominator)
